<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξερημόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make quite desolate,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. οἶκον</span>
			<i>leave</i> it <i>destitute of heirs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				43.76
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Le.</u>
				26.31
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξερημῶσαι γένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1010
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. δόμους</span>
			<i>abandon</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				597
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				991
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεις -ωμένας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					332e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τὰ ἑαυτῶν</span>
			<i>leaving</i> their own places <i>destitute</i> (of troops),
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Vect.</u>
				4.47
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δράκοντος γένυν ἐ.</span>
			<i>making</i> it <i>destitute</i> of teeth, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				253
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be left destitute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλλὰς ἐξερημωθεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					647
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸν ἐξηρημωμένον . . οἶκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					925c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
